### Related context
- `LV_TEXT_FLAG_EXPAND` is also set by non-label callers of lv_draw_label: src/widgets/textarea/lv_textarea.c:1405 (placeholder), src/widgets/table/lv_table.c:836-837, src/widgets/roller/lv_roller.c:583. These use lv_draw_label_dsc_init (memzero) and never set the new `text_size` field.
- src/draw/nema_gfx/lv_draw_nema_gfx_label.c:433 has an identical EXPAND branch that was not changed.
- src/misc/lv_text.c: lv_text_get_next_line / lv_text_get_size override max_width to LV_COORD_MAX when LV_TEXT_FLAG_EXPAND is set (lines ~101, 210, 336, 346). Check whether `w` in lv_draw_label_iterate_characters matters under EXPAND (it is passed to lv_text_get_next_line; alignment uses lv_area_get_width(coords)).
- lv_label_set_long_mode (lv_label.c:~222-240) sets label->expand=1 for SCROLL, SCROLL_CIRCULAR, CLIP. get_label_flags at lv_label.c:1276. lv_label_refr_text is called on STYLE_CHANGED / SIZE_CHANGED and from all text setters.
- Old draw_main computed size with LV_COORD_MAX; the cached label->text_size is computed in lv_label_refr_text with max_w = content width. Check whether this differs under the flags in effect, and staleness scenarios (static text mutated, dots mode, text==NULL early return, font change via state).

